          <name>HAL_INIT_SLOT_MAP%s</name>
          <description>The adjacent words at 0x2010134c and 0x20101350 each hold eight independently initialized four-bit lanes. For every lane, the complete BTDM HAL loop clears nibble mask 0xc, then ORs 1 | ((global index &amp; 3) &lt;&lt; 1) through a fresh read. Bit one can therefore retain a pre-existing one. The hardware meaning of the words and values remains unknown.</description>
